        "original_id": "0248f34d-0e67-5fad-a332-5dc5456d76a0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Margarita Lozano, Luis Buñuel, Sergio Leone, Pier Paolo Pasolini, Paolo Taviani, Vittorio Taviani, Nanni Moretti, Claude Berri, Marcel Pagnol, Carmelo Gómez, Icíar Bollaín, Francisco Algora\n- Works: Viridiana, A Fistful of Dollars, Pigsty, The Night of the Shooting Stars, Kaos, Good Morning Babylon, La messa è finita, Jean de Florette, Manon of the Spring, Manon des Sources, Nos miran\n- Topics: film collaborations, film adaptations, French-language films\n\nFacts:\n- Margarita Lozano worked with Luis Buñuel in \"Viridiana.\"\n- Margarita Lozano worked with Sergio Leone in \"A Fistful of Dollars.\"\n- Margarita Lozano worked with Pier Paolo Pasolini in \"Pigsty.\"\n- Margarita Lozano worked with the Taviani brothers in \"The Night of the Shooting Stars,\" \"Kaos,\" and \"Good Morning Babylon.\"\n- Margarita Lozano worked with Nanni Moretti in \"La messa è finita.\"\n- Margarita Lozano appeared in Claude Berri's two-film project \"Jean de Florette\" and \"Manon of the Spring.\"\n- \"Manon des Sources\" is a 1986 French-language film.\n- Claude Berri directed \"Manon des Sources\" as the second of two films adapted from Marcel Pagnol's 1966 two-volume novel, which Pagnol based on his own earlier film of the same title.\n- \"Nos miran\" is a thriller starring Carmelo Gómez with Icíar Bollaín, Margarita Lozano, and Francisco Algora.",
